# LegalMind V1 — environment template
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env (S-6: secrets outside source
# control; keys rotatable). This file lists only variables the code actually
# reads — it invents nothing.
#
# Verify against: backend/legalmind/config.py

# ─── Database (backend/legalmind/config.py) ─────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL is the locked system of record (Step 39, 41.1).
# Databases are named legalmind_v1_* deliberately — see backend/README.md.
LEGALMIND_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:pass@127.0.0.1/legalmind_v1_dev
LEGALMIND_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:pass@127.0.0.1/legalmind_v1_test

# ─── NOT YET SPECIFIED — do not invent these ────────────────────────────────
#
# The following are required by locked decisions but their configuration
# mechanism is explicitly unspecified. Add each variable only when the
# corresponding decision is made — inventing a key name here would make an
# unspecified decision look settled (CLAUDE.md rule 8).
#
#   Session signing / cookie keys   `AM-36` (AB-8) closes this for the JWT
#                                   mechanism only — see LEGALMIND_JWT_SECRET
#                                   below. Cookie signing keys remain
#                                   NOT YET SPECIFIED
#   Object storage credentials      Step 39 locks S3-compatible storage; the
#                                   provider and layout are NOT YET SPECIFIED
#   Celery / Redis broker URL       locked in the stack table; no code reads it yet
#   Rate-limit thresholds           Step 49: deployment configuration
#   Retention policy settings       NOT YET SPECIFIED (41.26 defers it)

# ─── Corporate SSO / OIDC (Step 47 §47.1.3, OD-9; deployment prereq 55.6) ───
# Locked 47.1.3 makes corporate SSO via OIDC the PRIMARY mechanism and password
# login "a controlled fallback". Implemented 2026-09-01 in
# backend/legalmind/security/oidc.py — no JWT/JWKS dependency was needed, because
# the ID token is read from our own direct TLS exchange with the token endpoint
# and is never accepted from a client.
#
# All four are required together; with any of them unset SSO is refused and only
# the password fallback works. The deployment preflight reports it (55.6).
#
# Google Workspace values come from Google Cloud console → Google Auth Platform →
# Clients → (your Web application client).
LEGALMIND_OIDC_ISSUER=https://accounts.google.com
LEGALMIND_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# S-6 — a secret. Never committed, never logged. Google no longer allows viewing
# an existing secret; use "Add secret" on the client to mint a new one.
LEGALMIND_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must match the Authorized redirect URI registered on that client BYTE FOR BYTE,
# and must be the route this application serves. Deliberately NOT derived from the
# inbound Host header, which an attacker controls.
LEGALMIND_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=https://legalmind.lsnw.io/api/v1/auth/oidc/callback
# Restrict sign-in to one email domain. Enforced server-side against the verified
# email claim, not against Google's advisory `hd` parameter. Unset = no domain
# restriction (the account-must-already-exist rule is then the only gate).
LEGALMIND_OIDC_ALLOWED_DOMAIN=leapswitch.com
# Where a successful SSO sign-in lands. A path, never a full URL.
# LEGALMIND_OIDC_POST_LOGIN_PATH=/documents
# Just-in-time provisioning (owner instruction 2026-09-01). Roles granted to an
# account created on first SSO sign-in. `USER` is ordinary contract/review work and
# carries NONE of legal.decision, legal_position.view, user.manage or audit.view —
# an identity provider must never confer authority (SEC-01, SEC-02, ROLE-05).
#   DISABLED  = no provisioning; an unknown identity is refused
#   (empty)   = provision with no roles at all; an admin grants later
# LEGALMIND_OIDC_JIT_ROLES=USER


# --- JWT session tokens (AM-36, AB-8, locked 2026-09-01) ----------------------
# S-6 — a secret. HS256 signing key for the stateless session token. At least 32
# bytes or the process refuses to issue AND to verify (AM-36 t5: no downgrade).
# Rotating it invalidates every live token immediately, which is the ONLY blunt
# revocation this mechanism has — see AM-36 t4.
LEGALMIND_JWT_SECRET=

# --- Assist lane (AB-3/AB-4) -------------------------------------------------
# Schema for the assist tables (AM-27 r1). Tests derive a per-run value; deployments
# use the default. LEGALMIND_ASSIST_SCHEMA=assist
# Local embedding-model store (AM-26 r5; weights provisioned once via
# tools/provision_model.py and checksum-verified at load).
# LEGALMIND_MODEL_DIR=/var/lib/legalmind/models
# Generation (AM-30). The key is the ONLY provider secret; never committed, never
# logged. While the AM-31 gate is CLOSED, production egress is refused regardless of
# this key — development/staging (synthetic material only, locked 55.3) will call the
# provider when it is set.
# LEGALMIND_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# A DATED model pin — a floating alias like "-latest" is refused (AM-30 t7).
# LEGALMIND_GENERATION_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
